window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-49da96f87b34e882"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"audit-a-workflow\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">审查工作流</h1> <p>将混乱的流程整理成清晰的审计报告和自动化计划。</p> <p>向 ChatGPT 提供跟踪表、流程文档、交接记录、仪表板、工单历史、团队讨论和约束，然后请它梳理现有工作流、找出卡点，并起草可用于自动化的流程规范。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>包含重复人工步骤、职责不清或经常交接失败的运营流程。</li> <li>正在判断某个流程是否适合自动化的团队。</li> <li>需要一并记录当前步骤、卡点、缺少的数据和过期来源的审计。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>阅读流程文档、跟踪表、交接记录和来源材料。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>查看团队讨论、重复问题和有助于说明流程如何运行的决策。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>检查工作流跟踪表、时间戳、负责人和 KPI 数据。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>生成审计简报、更新后的流程文档和自动化规范。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>审计此工作流</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">审查 [workflow]（工作流名称），并在 [deadline or next cohort]（截止日期或下一批次）之前完成。\n\n使用我提供的当前跟踪表、流程文档、交接记录、KPI 仪表板、工单历史、团队讨论和工作流约束。请创建：\n\n- 一份工作流审计简报，列出现有步骤、负责人、卡点、重复问题和缺失数据\n- 一份更新后的流程文档\n- 针对最重复的两个手动步骤的简短自动化规范\n\n标出过期或彼此冲突的来源。自动化提案应保持范围精简；不要实施或发布任何改动。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/how-to-use-codex-for-everyday-work/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy：日常工作（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">计划任务</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">智能体技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"map-the-current-process\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">梳理当前流程</h2> <p>如果当前流程清楚明确，就更容易评估自动化。向 ChatGPT 提供能展示工作实际流转方式的跟踪表、流程文档、交接记录、工单、指标和讨论。</p> <ol> <li>定义工作流的边界、用户、输入、输出和审查日期。</li> <li>附上当前流程文档、跟踪表、交接记录、工单和 KPI 背景。</li> <li>请 ChatGPT 对照实际讨论和跟踪表状态，核查文档所述的流程。</li> <li>运行起步提示词，生成审计简报、流程文档和范围精简的自动化规范。</li> <li>在实施前审查权限、例外路径、不可逆操作和负责人。</li> </ol> <p>自动化提案应与流程说明分开。好的审计应说明哪些工作需要继续人工处理、哪些工作可以自动验证，以及新工作流必须生成哪些证据。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-the-smallest-useful-automation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">选择范围最小但有用的自动化</h2> <p>审计完成后，请 ChatGPT 根据重复频率、风险、数据质量和验证成本比较候选步骤。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Rank the automation candidates from this workflow audit.\n\nFor each candidate, show:\n\n- current manual effort and repetition\n- required inputs and permissions\n- failure and exception paths\n- verification artifact\n- reversibility and human approval point\n- reason to defer or automate\n\nRecommend only the smallest safe first step. Do not implement it or change the source process document.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">对这份工作流审计中的自动化候选项排序。\n\n对每个候选项，展示：\n\n- 当前的人工投入和重复程度\n- 所需输入和权限\n- 失败与异常处理路径\n- 验证产物\n- 可逆性和人工批准节点\n- 推迟实施或进行自动化的理由\n\n只推荐最小的安全起步动作。不要实施，也不要更改源流程文档。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"audit-a-workflow\">Audit a workflow</h1> <p>Turn a messy process into a clear audit and automation plan.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT trackers, process docs, handoff notes, dashboards, ticket history, team discussions, and constraints, then ask it to map the current workflow, identify stuck points, and draft an automation-ready process spec.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Operational workflows with repeated manual steps, unclear ownership, or frequent handoff failures.</li> <li>Teams deciding whether a process is ready for automation.</li> <li>Audits that need current steps, stuck points, missing data, and outdated sources documented together.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read process documentation, trackers, handoff notes, and source artifacts.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Review team discussion, repeated questions, and decisions that explain how the process runs.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Inspect workflow trackers, timestamps, ownership, and KPI data.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Produce the audit brief, updated process document, and automation spec.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Audit this workflow</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Audit the [workflow] before [deadline or next cohort].\n\nUse the current tracker, process documentation, handoff notes, KPI dashboard, ticket history, team discussion, and workflow constraints I provide. Create:\n\n- a workflow audit brief with current steps, owners, stuck points, repeated questions, and missing data\n- an updated process document\n- a short automation spec for the two most repetitive manual steps\n\nFlag outdated or conflicting sources. Keep the automation proposal narrow, and do not implement or publish changes.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/how-to-use-codex-for-everyday-work/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy: Everyday work (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Scheduled tasks</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"map-the-current-process\">Map the current process</h2> <p>Workflow automation is easier to evaluate when the current process is explicit. Give ChatGPT the tracker, process docs, handoff notes, tickets, metrics, and discussions that show how work actually moves.</p> <ol> <li>Define the workflow boundary, users, inputs, outputs, and review date.</li> <li>Attach the current process document, tracker, handoff notes, tickets, and KPI context.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to reconcile the documented process with observed discussion and tracker state.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt to produce the audit brief, process document, and narrow automation spec.</li> <li>Review permissions, exception paths, irreversible actions, and ownership before implementation.</li> </ol> <p>Keep the automation proposal separate from the process description. A good audit explains what should remain manual, what can be verified automatically, and what evidence the new workflow must produce.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-the-smallest-useful-automation\">Choose the smallest useful automation</h2> <p>After the audit, ask ChatGPT to compare candidate steps by repetition, risk, data quality, and verification cost.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Rank the automation candidates from this workflow audit.\n\nFor each candidate, show:\n\n- current manual effort and repetition\n- required inputs and permissions\n- failure and exception paths\n- verification artifact\n- reversibility and human approval point\n- reason to defer or automate\n\nRecommend only the smallest safe first step. Do not implement it or change the source process document.\n</code></pre>"};
